/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 75 0 R
/T (A smart home automation system is being designed to manage lighting, temperature, and security based on user behavior and environmental conditions. The system must respond to real-time inputs such as motion detection, temperature changes, and time of day while also learning user preferences over time. In this context, explain the different types of intelligent agents \(simple reflex, model-based, goal-based, and utility-based agents\) and analyze how each type would function within this system. Justify which type of agent or hybrid approach would be most effective for ensuring comfort, energy efficiency, and security.)
/E (A smart home automation system is being designed to manage lighting, temperature, and security based on user behavior and environmental conditions. The system must respond to real-time inputs such as motion detection, temperature changes, and time of day while also learning user preferences over time. In this context, explain the different types of intelligent agents \(simple reflex, model-based, goal-based, and utility-based agents\) and analyze how each type would function within this system. Justify which type of agent or hybrid approach would be most effective for ensuring comfort, energy efficiency, and security.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
