/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 76 0 R
/T (A utility-based agent selects actions by evaluating a utility function, which assigns a numeric score to each possible state of the world. Higher utility corresponds to a more desirable state. Rather than merely asking whether a goal has been achieved, the agent asks how desirable an outcome is. This allows it to make rational decisions even when goals conflict and to choose the best available action under uncertainty.)
/E (A utility-based agent selects actions by evaluating a utility function, which assigns a numeric score to each possible state of the world. Higher utility corresponds to a more desirable state. Rather than merely asking whether a goal has been achieved, the agent asks how desirable an outcome is. This allows it to make rational decisions even when goals conflict and to choose the best available action under uncertainty.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [12]
>>
