248 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 81 0 R
/T (UCS is complete, meaning it will always find a solution if one exists, provided the branching factor is finite and all step costs are strictly positive \(greater than zero\). UCS is also optimal: it always returns the minimum-cost path to the goal under non-negative step costs, because it expands nodes in order of increasing path cost and the goal is accepted only when it is dequeued, not when it is first generated.)
/E (UCS is complete, meaning it will always find a solution if one exists, provided the branching factor is finite and all step costs are strictly positive \(greater than zero\). UCS is also optimal: it always returns the minimum-cost path to the goal under non-negative step costs, because it expands nodes in order of increasing path cost and the goal is accepted only when it is dequeued, not when it is first generated.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
