250 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 81 0 R
/T (Iterative Deepening Search combines the memory efficiency of depth-first search with the completeness of breadth-first search. It works by repeatedly executing depth-limited depth-first search \(DLS\) with an increasing depth limit. In each iteration, DLS explores all nodes reachable within the current depth limit and returns failure if no goal is found. The depth limit is then incremented by 1 and the search is restarted from the beginning.)
/E (Iterative Deepening Search combines the memory efficiency of depth-first search with the completeness of breadth-first search. It works by repeatedly executing depth-limited depth-first search \(DLS\) with an increasing depth limit. In each iteration, DLS explores all nodes reachable within the current depth limit and returns failure if no goal is found. The depth limit is then incremented by 1 and the search is restarted from the beginning.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
