/Title (An intelligent agent is any entity that perceives its environment through sensors and acts upon that environment through actuators. The agent receives a sequence of percepts from the environment and produces actions in response. The collection of all percepts received so far is called the percept history. An agent program maps each possible percept sequence to an action, while an agent function mathematically describes the agent's behavior.)
