/Title (A simple reflex agent selects actions based solely on the current percept, ignoring all previous percepts. Its decision logic consists entirely of condition-action rules of the form: IF condition THEN action. It does not maintain any memory of past states and does not model the world; it simply matches the current percept to a rule and fires the corresponding action.)
