/Title (A model-based reflex agent overcomes partial observability by maintaining an internal state that summarizes what is currently happening in the environment. It uses two types of knowledge: a transition model \(how the world evolves over time\) and a sensor model \(how the world state is reflected in percepts\). By combining the internal state with the current percept, the agent can form a more complete picture of the environment before selecting an action.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 530 0 R
>>
