/Title (A goal-based agent acts in order to achieve a specified goal or set of goals. Rather than simply reacting to the current percept or internal state, it considers which actions will lead to a state in which the goal is satisfied. This requires some form of search or planning: the agent must look ahead and evaluate sequences of actions in order to find one that achieves the goal.)
