/Title (Iterative Deepening Search combines the memory efficiency of depth-first search with the completeness of breadth-first search. It works by repeatedly executing depth-limited depth-first search \(DLS\) with an increasing depth limit. In each iteration, DLS explores all nodes reachable within the current depth limit and returns failure if no goal is found. The depth limit is then incremented by 1 and the search is restarted from the beginning.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 548 0 R
/Next 562 0 R
>>
endobj
557 0 obj
<<
/Title (Within each DLS run, nodes are explored depth-first \(LIFO\). A visited list is maintained along the current path to prevent cycles on that path; nodes already on the current path are not re-expanded. After backtracking, a node may be visited again in a subsequent branch at the same depth limit.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 548 0 R
/Prev 563 0 R
>>
endobj
