/Title (UCS is complete, meaning it will always find a solution if one exists, provided the branching factor is finite and all step costs are strictly positive \(greater than zero\). UCS is also optimal: it always returns the minimum-cost path to the goal under non-negative step costs, because it expands nodes in order of increasing path cost and the goal is accepted only when it is dequeued, not when it is first generated.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 561 0 R
>>
endobj
