594 0 obj
<<
/Title (Uninformed search strategies, also called blind search strategies, explore the search space without using any domain-specific knowledge about the location of the goal. They do not possess a heuristic estimate of the distance remaining to the goal; they rely only on information available in the problem definition: the current state, the available actions, the transition model, the path cost, and the goal test. Both Uniform Cost Search \(UCS\) and Iterative Deepening Search \(IDS\) are uninformed strategies. They are called uninformed because they treat all unexplored states equally, without guiding the search towards the goal using a heuristic function such as estimated straight-line distance.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 585 0 R
>>
endobj
